IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `csa-formula`
IMPORT daydate

-- Child Support (Assessment) Act 1989, Part 5 (the formula, low income and minimum rates) and changing an assessment -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (the Regulations' reg 6 only). The published figures (annualised MTAWE figure, self-support amount, minimum
-- annual rate, low income rate, pension PP (single) maximum basic amount) are ILLUSTRATIVE inputs, not the gazetted ones,
-- and Jake's and Tahlia's incomes and nights are illustrative too: the scenario states none.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_child-support-assessment-act-1989_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `s 24 and reg 6 -- which children`

`Ruby in 2038` MEANS `My child` WITH
    `is an eligible child under sections 19 to 21` IS TRUE
    `is under 18` IS TRUE
    `is a member of a couple` IS FALSE
    `is in care under a child welfare law of Western Australia or South Australia` IS FALSE
    `is present in Australia, or an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident in Australia` IS TRUE

`a child in the CEO's care under WA child protection law` MEANS `My child` WITH
    `is an eligible child under sections 19 to 21` IS TRUE
    `is under 18` IS TRUE
    `is a member of a couple` IS FALSE
    `is in care under a child welfare law of Western Australia or South Australia` IS TRUE
    `is present in Australia, or an Australian citizen or ordinarily resident in Australia` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `Can child support be assessed for my child` `Ruby in 2038`
#ASSERT NOT `Can child support be assessed for my child` `a child in the CEO's care under WA child protection law`

