§ `ss 35, 40C, 40D, 65A, 66 -- how much must I pay`

-- Life event k071 (Jake, 15 June 2038): separated from Tahlia, Ruby is 5 and lives with her mother; Jake has her every
-- second weekend (52 nights a year). Illustrative incomes: Jake 70,000, Tahlia 50,000. By hand: child support incomes 40,000
-- and 20,000, combined 60,000; income percentage 66.67; care 14% (52/365 = 14.25, rounded down), cost percentage 24; child
-- support percentage 42.67; costs of the child 17% x 45,000 + 15% x 15,000 = 9,900; 42.67% x 9,900 = 4,224.33 -> 4,224.
`Jake in 2038 (k071)` MEANS `My child support case` WITH
    `my adjusted taxable income` IS 70_000
    `the other parent's adjusted taxable income` IS 50_000
    `the self-support amount` IS 30_000
    `the annualised MTAWE figure` IS 90_000
    `nights the children are in my care` IS 52
    `nights the children are in the other parent's care` IS 313
    `children aged 0 to 12` IS 1
    `children aged 13 or over` IS 0
    `I received an income support payment in the last relevant year of income` IS FALSE
    `the pension PP (single) maximum basic amount` IS 30_000
    `the minimum annual rate of child support` IS 550
    `the low income annual rate` IS 1_800
    `the Registrar has determined that section 65A does not apply to me` IS FALSE
    `a departure determination, departure order or child support agreement sets the rate` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `What is my income percentage` `Jake in 2038 (k071)` EQUALS 66.67
#ASSERT `What is my child support percentage` `Jake in 2038 (k071)` EQUALS 42.67
#ASSERT (`How much child support must I pay` `Jake in 2038 (k071)`)'s `how it is worked out` EQUALS `by the formula (s 35)`
#ASSERT (`How much child support must I pay` `Jake in 2038 (k071)`)'s `my annual rate for all the children` EQUALS 4224

